**The thesis if you do run it:** her commercial value in the 2010s was *legible spontaneity* — the goofy, unfiltered anti-model whose brand was that she wasn't performing. She's since said the paparazzi images of her at her worst were what sent her to rehab, and that sobriety was the "amazing catalyst" that finally let her make the music. The aristocrat from Belgravia built a career on being the chaotic un-posh one; the woman whose product was uninhibitedness found her voice only after she stopped. Sources are unusually deep — Vogue cover story, Rolling Stone music feature, Playboy, *Planet Sex*.

